    "units_merged": 26,
    "adjustments": [
     "Removed \"Ambad Bk.\" (33.0 km2): census tags it as NMC but it hangs off the far south (19.84-19.90 N) sharing only 12% of its border with the rest of the city; removing it brings the area from 292.7 to about 259.7 km2, matching the 259.13 km2 figure.",
     "Added the unnamed census polygon (7.2 km2) around Ambad / Ambad MIDC (about 19.957 N, 73.741 E): it shares 92% of its border with NMC units and Ambad is a city locality. With it the total is about 267 km2, matching the infobox figure.",
     "Filled three Govardhan slivers (0.15 km2 total) fully enclosed by the city; kept the 2.4 km2 Dhondegaon enclave as a hole because the census does not tag it as NMC."
    ],
    "caveats": "Still built from 2011 census village units, not the official NMC limit. Matching the published area is supporting evidence, not proof. Verify against NMC ward GIS before using for legal or area calculations.",
    "source": "Census of India 2011 village boundaries via DataMeet (ODbL)",
    "generated_on": "2026-10-20"
   },
